            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0359" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/6</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in Russia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-06T10:00:00+02:30">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 6, 1914, 10 a.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11:30 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Department’s August 4, 7 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d101-f1"/> Have asked audience
                    through Minister for Foreign Affairs stating reason. He replied offer comes too
                    late for Russia, should have been made earlier. Austria only country where it
                    can help now. Audience with the Emperor uncertain on account of numerous
                    engagements and approaching departure for Moscow where he will remain some
                    time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
